-- title:
--   Exact parameters for the 2.0205 finite sensitivity certificate
-- statement:
--   Set
--   $$M=1475863,\quad r=88,\quad K=1439236,\quad d=17,\quad L=19,\quad k=2M^2+1.$$
--   Let $(a,b,c,e)=\mathrm{sharpBounds}(M,r,L,d)$, using the simultaneous four-profile recurrence. Define the natural numbers
--   $$A=\max(Ka,b),\qquad B=KMk^{17}.$$
--   These are the constants `sharpM`, `sharpR`, `sharpK`, `sharpA`, and `sharpB`. The depth $17$ and base budget $19$ occur explicitly in the latter two definitions. This bundle records exact integers, without making numerical inequalities axioms. Later kernel-checked arithmetic proves the labeling condition $k^{16}<r^{104}$ and the strict comparison $A^{4041}<B^{2000}$, corresponding to exponent $4041/2000=2.0205$.
